# Option A: the Kali rolling repo as an ORDINARY, PINNED package source.
# Goes to /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kali.list. Paired with kali-pin.pref
# (priority 100) so it NEVER overrides the Debian base/libc - it only supplies
# the ~6 tools absent from Debian main. No Kali branding reaches the image.
# The signing key is installed via the paired kali.key.chroot (materialized by
# build-iso.sh at build time from https://archive.kali.org/archive-key.asc).
# live-build installs that key into the chroot's trusted keyring BEFORE it runs
# apt-get update on this source, so no `signed-by=` path is used (an includes.chroot
# keyring would land too late - after the archive apt-update). It is public info,
# not a credential, and the kali-pin.pref (prio 100) keeps it package-source-only.
deb http://http.kali.org/kali kali-rolling main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
